no-OS is provided, by default, under the permissive:

	SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause

as found in LICENSES/preferred/BSD-3-Clause (the repository's canonical
copy, with the Analog Devices copyright line, is LICENSE_BSD).

In addition, other licenses apply to specific files and directory trees.
The authoritative license for any file is the one declared in that file's
own header (an SPDX-License-Identifier tag or a license header).

The full text of every license used by Analog Devices' own no-OS code is
collected under LICENSES/, grouped by role:

	LICENSES/preferred/    licenses to use for new code
	LICENSES/permissive/   permissive, allowed, but not the default
	LICENSES/proprietary/  vendor device APIs; non-permissive

Bundled third-party libraries under libraries/ each carry their own
LICENSE / COPYING file in their directory.

For how licenses are declared and the repository-local LicenseRef-
identifiers used for proprietary vendor device-API code, see:

	doc/sphinx/source/license_rules.rst

The mere aggregation of these files (putting them side by side in one
source repository) does not create a single master license for all of
them. When you build a project that combines files, it is up to you to
ensure the individual licenses are compatible. Some proprietary ADI
vendor-API trees forbid combination with incompatible code outright, and
you may not distribute a binary that violates the terms of any file it
includes.

Nothing in this file restricts, limits, or supersedes the license terms of
any particular file.
